---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const op = {
  title: "Case Study: How a Paid Media Restructure Cut Cost-Per-Lead 30% and Lifted ROAS to 5.5x | Vamshidhar Reddy",
  description: "A client account that had quietly degraded: cost-per-lead creeping toward Rs.1,100, ROAS parked at 3.2x. By consolidating 40+ ad groups, moving to target-CPA bidding and A/B testing creatives, cost-per-lead fell to Rs.770 and ROAS reached 5.5x. Here is exactly what changed.",
  canonical: "https://vamshidharm.vercel.app/blog/case-study-restructuring-paid-media-cut-cpl-30.html",
  ogImage: "",
  variant: 'sub',
  active: "blog/case-study-restructuring-paid-media-cut-cpl-30.html",
};
const body = "<section class=\"wrap\"><article class=\"article\"><a class=\"back\" href=\"https://vamshidharm.vercel.app/blog.html\">← All posts</a><div class=\"ameta\"><b>Case Study</b><span>2026-08-07</span><span>7 min read</span></div><h1>Case Study: How a Paid Media Restructure Cut Cost-Per-Lead 30% and Lifted ROAS to 5.5x</h1><p>This is the kind of account every media buyer has met: a lot of ads running, a rising cost-per-lead, and a ROAS that stopped improving months ago. The client wanted cheaper leads and more revenue — not a lecture. Here's the work.</p><h2>The starting point</h2><p>Cost-per-lead sat around Rs.1,100 and ROAS was parked at 3.2x. The account had grown without a clean-up: over 40 ad groups, overlapping keywords competing against each other, no consistent bidding strategy, and creatives that had never been properly split-tested.</p><h2>What was actually wrong</h2><p>Three problems, none of them unique. First, too many tiny ad groups meant the budget was scattered and the bidding algorithm had no data to optimise. Second, without a target-based bid, the machine chased volume instead of qualified leads. Third, heroes were guesses — a headline with no A/B data is not a decision, it's a hope wearing a budget.</p><h2>The fix, in order</h2><ul><li><b>Consolidated 40+ ad groups</b> into tight, themed structures so budget aligned with intent</li><li><b>Moved to target-based bidding</b> so the algorithm had a single number to optimise for</li><li><b>Started A/B testing creatives</b> and shifted spend to the winner instead of splitting evenly</li></ul><h2>The result</h2><p>Cost-per-lead dropped from Rs.1,100 to Rs.770 — roughly a 30% reduction — and ROAS lifted from 3.2x to 5.5x on the same budget. Across the wider program the work also contributed around 15% organic traffic growth and over 70 qualified leads a month.</p><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(240px,1fr));gap:16px;margin:22px 0 6px\"><div style=\"background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:18px 20px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:1px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)\"><b style=\"color:var(--accent2)\">Cost per lead</b> &middot; Rs. per qualified lead</p><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px\"><div><div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:5px\"><span>Before restructure</span><b style=\"color:var(--txt)\">Rs.1,100</b></div><div style=\"height:14px;border-radius:7px;background:var(--card2);overflow:hidden\"><div style=\"width:100%;height:100%;background:var(--muted);border-radius:7px\"></div></div></div><div><div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:5px\"><span>After restructure</span><b style=\"color:var(--accent2)\">Rs.770</b></div><div style=\"height:14px;border-radius:7px;background:var(--card2);overflow:hidden\"><div style=\"width:70%;height:100%;background:var(--grad);border-radius:7px\"></div></div></div></div><p style=\"margin:14px 0 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--accent2)\"><b>−30%</b> cost-per-lead</p></div><div style=\"background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:18px 20px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:1px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)\"><b style=\"color:var(--accent2)\">ROAS</b> &middot; return on ad spend</p><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px\"><div><div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:5px\"><span>Before</span><b style=\"color:var(--txt)\">3.2x</b></div><div style=\"height:14px;border-radius:7px;background:var(--card2);overflow:hidden\"><div style=\"width:58%;height:100%;background:var(--muted);border-radius:7px\"></div></div></div><div><div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:5px\"><span>After</span><b style=\"color:var(--accent2)\">5.5x</b></div><div style=\"height:14px;border-radius:7px;background:var(--card2);overflow:hidden\"><div style=\"width:100%;height:100%;background:var(--grad);border-radius:7px\"></div></div></div></div><p style=\"margin:14px 0 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--accent2)\"><b>3.2x &rarr; 5.5x</b> on the same budget</p></div></div><blockquote>More budget doesn't fix a broken account. Structure does.</blockquote><h2>The takeaway</h2><p>The lessons are boring and powerful: consolidate so the data is clear, bid toward the target you actually care about, and test creatives instead of guessing. It's the same logic I bring to SEO and CRO — remove friction, give the machine a target, and let the numbers decide. If you've got an account that's plateaued, <a href=\"https://vamshidharm.vercel.app/contact.html\">let's talk</a>.</p><hr style=\"margin:36px 0;border:none;border-top:1px solid var(--line)\"/><p style=\"color:var(--muted)\"><b style=\"color:var(--accent2)\">Vamshidhar</b> — performance marketer who builds AI tools. Open to work. <a href=\"https://vamshidharm.vercel.app/contact.html\">Contact →</a></p></article></section>";
---
<Base {...op}>
  <Fragment set:html={body} />
  
</Base>
